{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoEnvelopeWiring","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoEnvelopeWiring","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoBranchPinned","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmDeriv"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.re_dVdy_mul_eq_zero_of_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.re_dVdy_mul_eq_zero_of_real","kind":"theorem","line":324,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeWiring.lean#L324-L343","doc":"**Hence the envelope condition holds at any curve point with a REAL root and\na real derivative** — which is exactly the positive real root's situation.\n\n`dVdy · y = 2πi·k` makes `dVdy` purely imaginary when `y` is real, and a real\n`Y'` then leaves nothing in the real part. This is Route 30's leak, discharged\nrather than assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exists_int_dVdy_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exists_int_dVdy_mul","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeWiring.lean#L294-L322","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.curve_eq_zero_of_saddle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.curve_eq_zero_of_saddle","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeWiring.lean#L271-L277","doc":"The exponentiated saddle condition **is** the curve. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.dVdy_eq_zero_iff_exp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.dVdy_eq_zero_iff_exp","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeWiring.lean#L251-L269","doc":"**`∂V/∂y = 0` reduces to the deformed saddle equation.**\n\n`dVdy = 0` says `log[(1−y)(1−x·y)(1−y/x)] = 2 log(−y)`; exponentiating and\nclearing `x` gives `x·y² = (1−y)(1−x·y)(x−y)`, which\n`deformed_saddle_iff_curve` identifies with the curve. Stated at the level of\nthe exponentiated identity, which is where the branch choice stops mattering. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.re_mul_eq_zero_of_im_axis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.re_mul_eq_zero_of_im_axis","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeWiring.lean#L242-L247","doc":"**The mechanism, named.** A purely imaginary `∂V/∂y` against a real `y′`\nleaves nothing in the real part — which is exactly the positive real root's\nsituation, where `∂V/∂y = 2πi/t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_re_deformedV_envelope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_re_deformedV_envelope","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeWiring.lean#L224-L240","doc":"**The envelope collapse for `Re V` — the one the transport uses.**\n\nThe hypothesis is not `∂V/∂y = 0` but the weaker `Re(∂V/∂y · y′) = 0`, which is\nwhat actually holds at all three roots: at the two non-real ones `∂V/∂y` is `0`\noutright, and at the positive real root `t` it is `2πi/t`, so `∂V/∂y · t′` is\npurely imaginary because `t` and `t′` are real. See the module docstring — the\nstronger hypothesis is false at that root, and Route 30 G2 measures it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_re","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_re","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeWiring.lean#L219-L222","doc":"Taking real parts of a `ℝ → ℂ` derivative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_deformedV_envelope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_deformedV_envelope","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeWiring.lean#L203-L215","doc":"**The envelope collapse.** With `∂V/∂y = 0`, the `Y′` term dies and the total\nderivative is the `x`-part alone — whatever `Y′` happens to be. This is why the\nargument needs only that the roots are *differentiable*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_deformedV_path","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_deformedV_path","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeWiring.lean#L166-L201","doc":"**The total derivative along any differentiable path.**\n\nFour applications of the one-variable chain rule, collected by `dV_collect`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_log_neg_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_log_neg_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeWiring.lean#L136-L162","doc":"**Route 2: `Y` real and positive — where route 1 is impossible.**\n\nAt `y = t > 0` the point `−t` is a *negative real*, so it lies on `log`'s cut and\n`hslit` can never hold. Route 30 G2 already showed the consequence for\n`∂V/∂y`; Route 31 G4 showed the sharper one — a statement carrying `hslit` is\n**vacuous** at the positive real root, which on this arc is one of the three\nroots at every single `φ`.\n\nThe derivative still exists along a *real* path, because `log(−t) = log t + iπ`\nis smooth in `t`, and it has the same value `Y′/Y`, so the path theorem below\ndoes not care which route supplied it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_log_neg_of_slitPlane","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasDerivAt_log_neg_of_slitPlane","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeWiring.lean#L128-L134","doc":"Route 1: `−y` off the cut. The generic case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.log_neg_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.log_neg_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeWiring.lean#L121-L126","doc":"`log(−r) = log r + iπ` for real `r > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.dV_collect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.dV_collect","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeWiring.lean#L107-L117","doc":"**The collection step, with the logarithms held opaque.**\n\n`L₁, L₂, L₃, M` stand for `log(1−y)`, `log(1 − x·y)`, `log(1 − y/x)`, `log(−y)`.\nKeeping them as variables is not stylistic: `field_simp` rewrites `1 − y/x` to\n`(x−y)/x`, and inside a logarithm that changes the branch. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.dVdy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.dVdy","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeWiring.lean#L100-L103","doc":"`∂V/∂y = [−log(1−y) − log(1 − x·y) − log(1 − y/x) + 2·log(−y)] / y`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.dVdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.dVdx","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeWiring.lean#L96-L98","doc":"`∂V/∂x = [−log(1 − x·y) + log(1 − y/x)] / x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.deformedV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.deformedV","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoEnvelopeWiring.lean#L92-L94","doc":"The deformed potential. ","signatureChunk":0}]}